> then use Elbereth to ward off the lich. [...]

It turned out that I could handle them, but in the
reverse order. Somewhere around dlvl:22 I found a
cockatrice that left a corpse, so I had put on some
unindentified gloves (uncursed as it turned out)
and tried to run to reach dlvl:10 before the corpse
decays. Alas, the dungeon paths were twisted, and
even spending some wand of digging charges to
shorten the paths did not prevent the corpse from
vanishing around dlvl:16. Down again one or two
levels and another cockatrice left a corpse. This
one was still intact when I reached the critical
level. Burned the E-word, waited, and stoned the
arch-lich. The minotaur left the level; trying to
come close he fell through the hole I dug to the
level below. So I descended, waited at the stairs
to give him one hit (while he during the same time
hit me a lot and hard), and immediately retreated
to heal. I needed a couple hit-leave-heal rounds
until he finally fell.

> 
